    {
      "id": 13537,
      "hub_id": null,
      "version": "3.0.4",
      "description": "<p><strong>Update Changelog:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Improved cloud terrain shadow intensity, you should always get a shadow now when the sun is behind a cloud (the shadow intensity will be based on the density of the part of the cloud the sun is behind)</li>\n<li>Fixed an issue where the shadows being casted by the clouds were reversed, i.e. if the sun was behind a cloud in front of you on the right of the screen, you would get a shadow on the left rather than on the right</li>\n<li>Adjusted some shader values to improve the look of the clouds (reminder you can adjust pretty much everything I do if you enable the advanced bepinex settings)</li>\n<li>Adjusted default wind values, clouds should move a bit faster now</li>\n<li>Added settings to adjust the min and max wind speed. Max speed is when tarkov’s wind is at its strongest, min obviously when it’s at its lowest. Tarkov’s wind changes dynamically. So, keep in mind, if you make the gap between these speeds too small/big you may have some strange side effects</li>\n<li>Various performance optimizations to the shader that may or may not help to keep your GPU from melting</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>WARNING: Updates to this mod will always reset your config for it due to changes to the shader and other things requiring config values to be adjusted.</strong></p>\n",
