    {
      "id": 13498,
      "hub_id": null,
      "version": "3.0.0",
      "description": "<p><strong>NOTE:</strong> Pictures in the imgur link in description have been updated to show the latest clouds</p>\n<p><strong>Update Changelog:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Rewrote the shader pretty much from the ground up again</li>\n<li>New and improved lighting on all aspects - ambient scattering, cloud density, shading</li>\n<li>Perspective/scale actually feels proper now</li>\n<li>WAY more variety in cloud shapes/position</li>\n<li>Randomized cloud wind direction every start of raid</li>\n<li>Removed clouds from maps that shouldn’t have clouds (this includes factory)</li>\n<li>Improved high clouds, they just look better and their coverage increases/decreases along with cumulus clouds</li>\n<li>Ambient color is now pulled directly from the sky and it has made the clouds blend with the sky way better</li>\n<li>Ground shadows! Yes, the clouds now will cast shadows on the ground (sometimes it takes a few seconds at raid start to kick in, this happens on base tarkov too, not sure why it happens)</li>\n<li>So much more that I can’t think of</li>\n</ul>\n",
