    {
      "id": 13324,
      "hub_id": null,
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "description": "<p><strong>NOTE: If you run VR and are struggling with performance, this might not be good to use. Use the 2D clouds version 1.0.7. You could also try lowering the primary steps to 32-48 and light steps to 8-12. Anything lower and it’s just not worth it.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Update Changelog:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Rewrote the shader from the ground up and is now using ray marched volumetrics</li>\n<li>Simplified the scripting of the clouds due to them being physically based, very little custom controller work is needed</li>\n<li>Added a config menu in f12, most settings are hidden in advanced, including where you can increase volumetric quality steps even higher. I hid them to avoid people crashing their PC’s. All the other settings, I don’t recommend touching unless you want to try improving the look of them, a lot of the settings are <em>very</em> sensitive</li>\n</ul>\n",
      "link": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/download/2567/cloudsix-volumetric-clouds/2.0.0",
      "content_length": 4548740,
      "spt_version_constraint": "4.0.13",
